    "body": "Selection gestures from [issue #90](https://github.com/ManuelSe/Neistra/issues/90), implemented in [PR #105](https://github.com/ManuelSe/Neistra/pull/105) under the [approved plan](https://github.com/ManuelSe/Neistra/blob/master/docs/plans/issue-90-selection-gestures.md).\n\n## Selection improvements\n\n- Ctrl/Cmd toggles complete operands across the viewer, project browser, groups, components/categories and existing Sequence tab. Partial selections become complete; unrelated atoms remain selected.\n- Unmodified Atom-mode double-click expands to one protein residue or assigned individual nonpolymer component, including a ligand inside a complex.\n- Viewer Shift-picks add inclusive protein-residue ranges from a fixed application-owned start in normalized source order. Gaps and insertion codes work without residue-number arithmetic; hidden existing atoms/H are included.\n\n## Changed gestures and fixes\n\nCtrl/Cmd now removes a fully selected operand instead of only adding. Alt subtracts; Ctrl/Cmd takes precedence over Shift. Plain clicks still replace and unmodified empty-space clicks clear. Single clicks remain immediate. Camera, navigation, movement ownership, explicit add/subtract and cross-panel synchronization retain their behavior. Delayed entry/group picks cannot publish into another project visit or stale artifact. See the [gesture guide](https://github.com/ManuelSe/Neistra/blob/master/docs/SELECTION_GESTURES.md).\n\n## Scientific boundaries and limitations\n\nCanonical component/residue identity defines membership. No molecule discovery from proximity, chemistry inference, missing-residue reconstruction, coordinate edits or original-file rewriting. Protein ranges require the same entry, protein component and chain. Unsupported/ambiguous polymers retain ordinary picks and existing warnings. Anchors survive valid responsive remounts but clear on reload, replacement, mode/project/artifact change or incomplete start membership. No dedicated touch double-tap/profile system is introduced; keyboard-operable panels and explicit picking/expansion remain available.\n\n## API/data compatibility and migrations\n\nStable minor0.22.0 updates all five authoritative version sources. It adds useful capabilities and intentionally changes modifier behavior while retaining HTTP and persisted contracts. No database migration, dependency upgrade or durable gesture fields: Alembic0014, normalized/selection1, project/viewer/archive2 remain. Named selections/scenes store ordinary canonical references; anchors are transient. Actual tagged0.21 API/core/plugin readers retain final0.22 data, originals, coordinates, viewer settings, selections/scenes, surfaces, generic Undo/Redo and jobs;0.22 readers accept0.21 archives. Archives retain current state and intentionally omit command history. Older readers do not gain gesture authoring. Back up managed data before application rollback; no issue-specific conversion is required.\n\n## Verification\n\nClean candidate7dc4340 and exact merged master28d3a9bb59c6e786e0586ae589f0e0ebfee7678a each pass all15 commands: **1,107 Python,290 frontend,8 supervisor,282 browser /52 existing intentional layout/timing exclusions**, zero failures/flakes/retries/native scientific skips. Frozen installs, fresh0014 migration, Ruff, mypy91, ESLint, TypeScript, build, five-version/provenance and diff checks pass. All472 runtime/test/tool identities match. Actual tagged-reader checks pass both directions. All14 new native gesture cases, both-theme full-shell axe, keyboard/touch ownership and actual100%/200%browser zoom pass.\n\nPinned1STP1001 candidate measurements: import/viewer1154ms, interactions3861ms, longest task652ms, zero repeated normalized requests. Exact merged measurements: import/viewer699ms, interactions4473ms, longest task655ms, zero repeated normalized requests. Unchanged movement, surface and18k minimization budgets pass; these are host regression gates rather than general throughput promises. Existing Alembic deprecation and lazy-bundle advisories remain.\n\nThe attached verification ZIP retains commands, source hashes, lossless logs, timing attachments, archives, review and a checksum manifest. Earlier raster/readiness diagnostics are distinguished from passing final evidence. Review is local implementer self-review; `@codex review` was requested but no independent review returned, and no required approval/check/protection was bypassed.\n\n## Follow-up work\n\nHover highlighting remains[#91](https://github.com/ManuelSe/Neistra/issues/91); component residue navigation/shared ranges remain[#94](https://github.com/ManuelSe/Neistra/issues/94); a docked sequence viewer remains[#95](https://github.com/ManuelSe/Neistra/issues/95). Existing panels share toggles but do not establish range starts. No duplicate follow-up was created. Geometry-based molecule inference, persisted anchors, viewer-owned selection and new backend/framework/schema proposals were rejected because canonical application infrastructure is sufficient. Dedicated double-tap/configurable profiles were omitted as optional scope.\n"
